      "id": 1,
      "text": "Linntown takes its name from the Linn family, who owned several farms on the south side of the turnpike.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Linntown%2C_Pennsylvania"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The arrival of the railroad in Linntown stimulated commercial ventures like the Kulp Lumber Mill and the Lewisburg Chair Factory.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Linntown%2C_Pennsylvania"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Linntown's early roots are tied to the nineteenth-century linen industry, which relied on flax grown along the Penns Creek floodplain.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
